{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1090903-the-five-exclusive-modes-of-lunar-combat","id":1090903,"title":"The five \"exclusive\" modes of Lunar combat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-10T16:04:05-07:00","id":1090903,"title":"The five \"exclusive\" modes of Lunar combat","content":"Right now, I can think of five broad paths for Lunar Exalted Charms to take in regards to combat style, each of which would be balanced against the others.<br /> <br /> I don't see these as exclusive in the sense that you can build towards only one, or that you can't use more than one of them in a single fight, but rather that you can only use one of these tactics in any given moment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>1) Human form.</b> For those Lunar Exalted who wish to rely on all other Exalted gifts except the one unique to their own form of Exaltation. They specialize entirely in some combination of Artifacts and Evocations, Martial Arts Styles, Sorcery, and Attribute Charms.<br /> <br /> <b>2) &quot;War Form&quot; / Deadly Beastman Transformation.</b> Still capable of using Artifacts but less capable of Evoking their greater powers. Still capable of performing Martial Arts Styles design for humans, but with inhuman advantages and the possibility of inhuman Martial Arts Styles such as the Dragon King arts of Wing Dagger and Black Depths.<br /> <br /> <b>3) Towering Beast Form.</b> The power to shapeshift into a creature with the Legendary Size merit; balanced to prevent Lunars from abusing the power to become a giant whenever it is convenient. Balanced to be competitive with the option of using a War Form, keeping in mind that Towering Beast Form becomes much less useful in confined spaces. Generally cannot use most Artifacts or tools in general. Wing Dagger and Black Depths Styles are available to flying or swimming giants, but vanishingly few other Styles are available.<br /> <br /> <b>4) Constant shapeshifting.</b> Rather than relying on the advantages of human invention, or the raw power of DBT or TBF, a Lunar uses a Charm that discounts the cost of assuming any shape smaller than Legendary Size, so that they can fight by rapidly changing shapes.<br /> <br /> <b>5) &quot;Shadow Clone no Jutsu&quot;.</b> The Lunar answer to &quot;Faster Than Self Technique&quot;, the shapeshifter splits apart into a battle-group of stolen shapes and faces.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of the four of these avenues which require Charms to attempt, I think they can be neatly cut along Strength and Dexterity. Both Deadly Beastman Transformation and Towering Beast Form would be Strength Charms, and the other two paths would be Dexterity-based.<br /> <br /> Relentless Lunar Fury, as the Lunar answer to the Solar Resistance &quot;Rage&quot; Charms, would be Stamina-based as before, and fully compatible with ANY of the five modes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T16:54:15-07:00","id":1090925,"title":"","content":"I'll respond to each and then propose a 6th style:<br /> <br /> 1) Honestly I doubt this one will ever be perfectly balanced with the others. Will it be viable, I would like to think so. But it's unlikely it will be equal to the other options. The reason is simple math, all Lunar's can shapeshift. It doesn't matter if you choose not to, it's an inherent ability and is therefore always calculated into your overall &quot;power-level&quot;. The best in-game example would be Solar's Excellencies. All Solar's have at minimum 10 Excellencies even at chargen, possibly more. You can't ask the Devs to balance your Solar around not having Excellencies because you don't wish to use them, because you do have them. All Lunar's can shapeshift regardless of whether they use it or not. Now I do hope the &quot;human form&quot; build is viable for Lunar's, but I have doubts that it can be fairly balanced against the others.<br /> <br /> 2) I have nothing to add for DBT.<br /> <br /> 3) This will be a difficult one to balance as well. It might require some sort of in-combat power up system, or severe limitations on its use to be fair. Either way, I think this is a niche form of combat that likely won't see consistent use.<br /> <br /> 4) Nothing to add to your &quot;constant shapeshifter&quot;.<br /> <br /> 5) I'm not aware of any comments made on such abilities for Lunar's. Is the &quot;splitting apart&quot; something the Devs have mentioned? As it stands, turning your character into a battlegroup isn't something that the current rules would handle well. Several additional rules would need to be added to make this viable.<br /> <br /> Okay, you missed one type of combat the Devs have already said is possible:<br /> <br /> 6) Chimera Style - Using your shapeshifting to hybrid-ize yourself with the best characteristics of several creatures. A scorpions tail, a clawstriders feet claws, a gorillas powerful grasping hands, a fae creatures immolating hide, etc! The Devs said quite a while back that chimera's were changing drastically in 3E from insane Wyld-tainted monsters, to a willing choice by the Lunar to hybridize themselves that would be very useful in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","user":"TalosX","date":". 05-10-2017, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T20:00:00-07:00","id":1090968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1090903-the-five-exclusive-modes-of-lunar-combat?p=1090925#post1090925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Honestly I doubt this one will ever be perfectly balanced with the others. Will it be viable, I would like to think so. But it's unlikely it will be equal to the other options. The reason is simple math, all Lunar's can shapeshift. It doesn't matter if you choose not to, it's an inherent ability and is therefore always calculated into your overall &quot;power-level&quot;. The best in-game example would be Solar's Excellencies. All Solar's have at minimum 10 Excellencies even at chargen, possibly more. You can't ask the Devs to balance your Solar around not having Excellencies because you don't wish to use them, because you do have them. All Lunar's can shapeshift regardless of whether they use it or not. Now I do hope the &quot;human form&quot; build is viable for Lunar's, but I have doubts that it can be fairly balanced against the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the only form in which a Lunar can make the most use of the vast majority of Artifacts. Deadly Beastman Transform may render them Dissonant with even moonsilver, if it doesn't lock them out of everything but attunement bonuses. Fully bestial forms don't even have hands!<br /> <br /> The ability to mix Evocations and martial arts Styles is not to be sneezed at.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) This will be a difficult one to balance as well. It might require some sort of in-combat power up system, or severe limitations on its use to be fair. Either way, I think this is a niche form of combat that likely won't see consistent use. </div> </div> </div>Dude, we're just talking about the ability to turn into an elephant or a dinosaur. At most, it's just going to be more expensive than shapeshifting into smaller forms, and possibly with a mote-tax every round that you remain huge.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5) I'm not aware of any comments made on such abilities for Lunar's. Is the &quot;splitting apart&quot; something the Devs have mentioned? As it stands, turning your character into a battlegroup isn't something that the current rules would handle well. Several additional rules would need to be added to make this viable. </div> </div> </div>After &quot;Miracles of the Solar Exalted&quot; released the backer Charm &quot;Faster Than Self Technique&quot;, Vance admitted that turning into a battle group was a naturally Lunar trick.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6) Chimera Style - Using your shapeshifting to hybrid-ize yourself with the best characteristics of several creatures. A scorpions tail, a clawstriders feet claws, a gorillas powerful grasping hands, a fae creatures immolating hide, etc! </div> </div> </div>That's just using Deadly Beastman Transformation or Towering Beast Form with a twinked out shape. It's not meaningfully different from either of those two modes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T21:22:36-07:00","id":1090976,"title":"","content":"You're missing my point on human-form combat. It's not that I don't believe its a viable choice. Rather its difficult to balance a splat based solely around someone who doesn't want to use part of that splats abilities. As for Evocations, the Devs have said repeatedly that Dissonant wasn't going to be a heavy penalty. Until we see one way or the other, it's difficulty to judge just how much those Evocations are going to improve/limit Lunar-form choices.<br /> <br /> With Towering Beast Form, if they increase it's shifting cost and add a mote-tax, then my comment stands. It's not a form you're going to hop into and fight through several scenes spanning an hour or two of game time. If it's not something you can maintain, it's something you use in niche situations.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;Beast Menagerie Transformation&quot; (just making that up on the fly) there's still a lot of questions that would need to be clarified. The battlegroup rules currently don't cover some scenarios I see coming up. So either battlegroup rules would need to be expanded, or a Lunar sub-set would need to be created. Either way, it's an interesting concept.<br /> <br /> Comments made about Chimeras imply that its far more intensive then just &quot;twinking your shape&quot;. Also who said DBT form? Why not a lions body, with a long-necked venomous snake head, and bat wings? How about an octopus's body with a shark head and skin from an electric eel? Chimeras don't have to have anything to do with DBT, and might be incompatible with certain DBT abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","user":"TalosX","date":". 05-11-2017, 12:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T22:00:15-07:00","id":1090978,"title":"","content":"Or you could just have a good old fashion gorgon (human upper torso and face with snakes replacing the hair and a serpentine lower body).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T01:34:35-07:00","id":1091018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1090903-the-five-exclusive-modes-of-lunar-combat?p=1090978#post1090978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you could just have a good old fashion gorgon (human upper torso and face with snakes replacing the hair and a serpentine lower body).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, sounds like another option. You probably couldn't petrify with sight, but perhaps incorporate some exotic creatures poison to spit, or hypnotic eyes. A lot of fun stuff to do with chimeras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T09:02:26-07:00","id":1091154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1090903-the-five-exclusive-modes-of-lunar-combat?p=1090978#post1090978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you could just have a good old fashion gorgon (human upper torso and face with snakes replacing the hair and a serpentine lower body).</div> </div> </div> </div>Either the gorgon is a stolen form or it's just Deadly Beastman Transformation, right?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T12:04:12-07:00","id":1091219,"title":"","content":"Not really. Snake hair is not something you'd expect from a normal DBT. Now it might be a stolen form (probably of a God-Blooded), but with Chimerism it wouldn't have to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T01:25:26-07:00","id":1091456,"title":"","content":"The thing with DBT is its just cosmetics and fluff. The rules (at least as they currently stand) for DBT are in the EX3 Core with the Lunar antagonists. It gives some solid buffs, but the benefits of having teeth, claws, etc. is just fluff. You could describe attacking with them, but most GMs will probably rule it a stunt and award you that way. With a chimera, you could have the head of a fogshark and use it's &quot;Frenzied Bite&quot; ability, while simultaneously having a bears arms to use the &quot;Crushing Bear Hug&quot; ability. Chimera style combatants will be able to put together some really awesome and scary forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T07:01:31-07:00","id":1095115,"title":"","content":"One of the things I liked about Lunars in previous editions was (1e) Moonsilver Monkey Exercise and (2e) Relentless Lunar Fury where they had a significant but temporary boost to their competence that could deactivate on them mid-fight. The problem was that the combo system/charm type strongly encouraged them to power up at the start of the fight and end it before their charm timed out so the result was inelegant and made Lunars appear weak rather than having a reserve of strength that could rival the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> Also the way Moonsilver Monkey was described always made me imagine a character winding up and storing potential energy, which seemed like a better image for an Alchemical than a Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T13:54:10-07:00","id":1095226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1090903-the-five-exclusive-modes-of-lunar-combat?p=1090976#post1090976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Towering Beast Form, if they increase it's shifting cost and add a mote-tax, then my comment stands. It's not a form you're going to hop into and fight through several scenes spanning an hour or two of game time. If it's not something you can maintain, it's something you use in niche situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mote-tax isn't likely to come up outside of ridiculously large forms, though.<br /> <br /> The more sensible intermediary step is mote <i>commitment</i>, like a Martial Arts Form Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T14:04:41-07:00","id":1096023,"title":"","content":"This thread has me wondering about this comment from the Aura charms thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1093725-aura-charms?p=1094697#post1094697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a very important point, and one that we place great emphasis on. Any time we do something that increases the overall complexity of a Charm set, we also need to reduce complexity in other places throughout the Charm set so that the overall mental burden of tracking isn't just absurd.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm kinda hoping that this means there's ideas in the works that would integrate knacks and charms in the lunar charm set. I've never really been a fan of how 2E handled it. With that in mind, I really wonder how much of a role the special powers from the core will play (things that you can train your animal familiars to do but that they don't necessarily know by default) and how much emphasis will be placed on borrowing those abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T15:38:32-07:00","id":1096060,"title":"","content":"I doubt that Knacks will continue to be different from Lunar Charms, or at least isolated from the Lunar Charmset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T10:03:06-07:00","id":1096395,"title":"","content":"Yeah, with no combo rules there's no real difference between knacks and charms besides being in different trees... and if the writers wanted, they could still have them in different trees anyway (not sure if they would or not, but anyway. Probably depends).<br /> <br /> It's probably easier to write Lunar powers that involve shapeshifting (as many do!) if you don't have to worry about &quot;is this a charm or a knack&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T13:59:44-07:00","id":1097869,"title":"","content":"My placeholder rules for Lunars feature a lot of charms that confer the effects of Merits and Special Attacks they might have access to via animal forms. Some of these charms then allow the Lunar to reflexively shapeshift into an acquired form that shares this trait and/or offer an additional bonus if you're already in a form that lets you do what the charm does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T11:25:06-07:00","id":1098162,"title":"","content":"I really kinda want to see a dodge charm that involves shapeshifting into a tiny animal, a damage adder that involves shapeshifting into a bear or rino or clawstrider or similar, etc. <br /> <br /> I really want a shapeshifter duel to be a viable method of combat among lunars.<br /> <br /> Prob not limited to that though. I don't want lunars to be a one-trick-pony either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T11:58:18-07:00","id":1098176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1090903-the-five-exclusive-modes-of-lunar-combat?p=1098162#post1098162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really kinda want to see a dodge charm that involves shapeshifting into a tiny animal</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small\"> Lunar Exalted and the power of being small - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> SHAPESHIFTING (excerpts) A Lunar may pay four motes to assume any form it has taken. This transformation lasts indefinitely, until the Lunar reverts to his true human form (which is free and reflexive) or shifts into a different shape. Shapeshifting can be flurried, but not with an attack. Animals with Legendary Size are beyond the skill of most young Lunar shapeshifters, though this limitation can be overcome. DEXTERITY CHARMS (ideas) Humble Mouse Shape This presumes that the power to don the form of a creature with the Tiny Creature merit is initially locked, like Legendary Size. As a reminder, </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> a damage adder that involves shapeshifting into a bear or rino or clawstrider or similar, etc. </div> </div> </div>That's been my wish for the return of First Edition's Body-Breaking Kata.<br /> <br /> Not the mechanics, but the concept.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Prob not limited to that though. I don't want lunars to be a one-trick-pony either. </div> </div> </div>I'm trying to explore the possibility of Lunar Exalted fighting like RWBY's Blake Belladonna, or like Naruto, with Shadow Clones. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1097768-lunar-cloning-no-items-fox-only-final-destination\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...al-destination</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}